Local review patch: contain a secondary-start acknowledgement timeout
Base: reviewed m1n1 2460b604c6f016956ead711823605eea840c602e, after adapted 0003
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Retain the non-returning post-release containment. Static stacks do not make
it safe to reuse target_cpu or reset pointers while a released CPU is late.
The existing 100 ms poll is unchanged. Applies to every supported SoC.
No native execution or late-core/reset correctness is established here.

--- a/src/smp.c
+++ b/src/smp.c
@@ -207,4 +207,5 @@
     if (i >= 100)
-        printf("Failed!\n");
+        /* A late CPU can still consume target_cpu and the shared reset stacks. */
+        panic("SMP: CPU %d start timed out; refusing to reuse reset state\n", index);
     else
         printf("  Started.\n");
